= Entropy — Simple =

'''Entropy''' is a mathematical idea used in more than one field.

In information theory, entropy measures uncertainty in possible messages or outcomes.

In physics, entropy is related to how many microscopic states can produce the same large-scale state.

People often call entropy “disorder,” but that can be misleading.

Shannon entropy and thermodynamic entropy use similar mathematics, but they are not automatically the same physical quantity.

